; Regression: null may not be PASSED to a non-optional reference parameter
; (2026-08-27, the argument arm of the null-into-ref gate).
;
; report_null_into_ref# judges the four positions that carry a DECLARED type,
; and type_conformance_accepted# class 2 refuses an Option at those same four.
; An ARGUMENT is judged by neither, and deliberately so: `null` plans as
; `pointer[void]`, which types_compatible# accepts for every pointer and every
; ref parameter BY INTENT -- overload resolution rests on that. So the call
; resolved, planned, mangled and emitted in silence, and the callee held a
; reference its own declaration says cannot be null.
;
; Swept before the gate existed (tools/nullref/nullarg.py): 85 sites over 40
; declarations, plus 22 more that only the compiler could resolve, because a
; text tool cannot tell two same-named `make`s apart.
;
; The METHOD shape is the one tested here; the sibling shapes (a qualified
; static, a construction, and the `null as pointer[X]` spelling of the same
; null) are in xfail_null_into_ref_arg_shapes.scaly. The exit is the `?` form
; -- null_into_ref_arg_ok.scaly proves it for all of them.
;
; xfail: null passed to a non-optional reference parameter

define Alpha (k: int)
{
    init(k: int)
        set this.k: k

    function taken(this: ref[Alpha], other: ref[Alpha]) returns int
        this.k
}

function drive() returns int
{
    var al Alpha#(7)
    al.taken(null)
}

Console.println "unreachable"
